# Line-ending determinism for NayaPOWER.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# CI runs on Linux; most seats work on Windows. Without this file, a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true materialises CRLF in the working tree,
# while the committed blobs are LF. Any tool that regenerates a committed
# artifact then produces a diff that is almost entirely phantom line-ending
# churn.
#
# This was measured, not assumed. Regenerating the brain index layer on
# Windows produced ~8,400 changed lines across three files where the true
# change was ~15. Nine separate branches named variations on "fix brain
# index drift" failed before the cause was found.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary files and leave them alone.
# `eol=lf` pins text files to LF in the working tree on every platform, so
# the working tree matches what CI checks out and what the committed blobs
# store.
#
# Companion fix: tools/regenerate_brain_index.py writes through write_lf(),
# which passes newline="\n" explicitly rather than relying on the platform
# default. That fix makes the generator deterministic on its own; this file
# stops the same drift arriving from the checkout side.
#
# Guarded by: tests/test_brain_index_line_endings.py

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated index layer — gate-compared byte-for-byte against the committed
# tree by BRAIN-INDEX-FRESHNESS. Never let these drift on line endings.
BRAIN/REAL-TREE.json      text eol=lf
BRAIN/REAL-TREE.md        text eol=lf
BRAIN/NAYAPOWER-BRAIN-INDEX.json text eol=lf